            <ArticleTitle>Computer tomography imaging of an unusual cause of appendicitis: a case report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>467-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.3978/j.issn.2223-4292.2014.08.07</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Foreign body occlusion of appendices lumen is a quite rare cause of appendicitis due to foreign body. We present a case of a 63-year-old male who presented with right lower quadrant pain since 24 hours. Computed tomography (CT) demonstrated an acute appendicitis due to a metallic foreign body which was found to be a bullet.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
